      "id": 1,
      "text": "Cinco Ranch began as a cattle ranch and rice farm on Buffalo Bayou in the 1930s, founded by five families who named it Cinco Ranch.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/cinco-ranch-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community sits about 25 miles west of Houston and ten miles north of Richmond in northern Fort Bend County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/cinco-ranch-tx",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Cinco Ranch’s roots stretch back before Texas became a republic, with settlers establishing the area in the early 19th century.",
